# The owner's paths: a PR that touches one waits for @nycruslan to approve its head. The team's
# PRs come from its checks app, so the owner approves and merges them; one under the owner's own
# login can't be approved by them, so it's opened again through the app. GitHub reads this
# file from the PR's base branch. The `gate` check and the team's file guard read it too
# (.crew/scope.mjs), matching without regard to case. The last matching line wins, so a line
# with no owner gives that path back to the team.

# The owner's facts; drafts are the team's, for the owner to approve.
/content/ @nycruslan
/content/drafts/

# The team's setup, apart from its memory and notes.
/.crew/ @nycruslan
/.crew/sprint/
/.crew/STATE.md
/.github/ @nycruslan
/.githooks/ @nycruslan
/.mcp.json @nycruslan

# Instructions load wherever they are: a .claude folder's skills for work below it, as CLAUDE.md
# and AGENTS.md, even in the team's memory. Attributes pick merge drivers and filters.
.claude/ @nycruslan
/.claude/agent-memory/
/.claude/agent-memory/**/.claude/ @nycruslan
CLAUDE.md @nycruslan
CLAUDE.local.md @nycruslan
AGENTS.md @nycruslan
AGENTS.local.md @nycruslan
.gitattributes @nycruslan

# What the team is scored by, and the toolchain's settings. package.json's scripts are the
# owner's too; `gate` checks those, since dependencies in the same file are the team's.
/PRODUCT.md @nycruslan
/design/rubric.md @nycruslan
/design/brief.md @nycruslan
/design/calibration/ @nycruslan
/skills-lock.json @nycruslan
/biome.json @nycruslan
/biome.jsonc @nycruslan
/tsconfig.json @nycruslan
/knip.json @nycruslan
/knip.jsonc @nycruslan
/pnpm-workspace.yaml @nycruslan
/renovate.json @nycruslan
/renovate.json5 @nycruslan
/playwright.config.* @nycruslan
# Biome and knip skip what git ignores, and .npmrc changes how pnpm installs.
/.gitignore @nycruslan
/.npmrc @nycruslan
